+<parallel_by_default>
+## Parallel Delegation ÔÇö DEFAULT, NOT OPTIONAL
+
+**Your default mode is PARALLEL fan-out. Sequential is the EXCEPTION.**
+
+For every batch of remaining tasks, the question is NOT "should I parallelize these?" ÔÇö it is **"What is BLOCKING me from firing all of them in ONE message?"**
+
+A task is sequential ONLY if it has a NAMED blocking dependency:
+- **Input dependency**: Task B reads what Task A produced (file, value, schema)
+- **File conflict**: Task A and Task B modify the same file
+
+Anything else ÔåÆ fire ALL of them in the SAME response, IN PARALLEL. One message, multiple `task()` calls.
